{"id":1446,"date":"2020-11-27T19:19:35","date_gmt":"2020-11-28T03:19:35","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1446"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:36","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:36","slug":"program-the-serial-read","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-serial-read\/","title":{"rendered":"Program the Serial Read"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215f9dd17f\" name=\"6a2215f9dd17f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Setup<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]For this lesson, you&#8217;re going to be sending a message from your computer to your Smart Inventor Board. Because you&#8217;ll be reading serial data, you will need to program the serial monitor. To start doing that, type the line below within\u00a0void setup()\u00a0.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">Serial.begin(57600);<\/pre>\n<p>This line of code sets the baud rate, which is the amount of bits per second that your Smart Inventor Board will be sending data to your computer.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215f9dd284\" name=\"6a2215f9dd284\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Serial.begin()<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">Serial.begin(BAUD rate);<\/pre>\n<p>Flashback to the last lesson!\u00a0This function creates a high-transfer\u00a0baud\u00a0connection between the\u00a0remote controller\u00a0and the\u00a0Smart Inventor Board. A higher baud number means the board will process information faster, but there&#8217;s also a higher chance for errors.\u00a0A lower\u00a0baud number means the board will process information slower, but there will also be less of a chance for errors.<\/p>\n<p>Baud rates range anywhere from 300 to 250000. Make sure that your baud rate is a number that is found within the drop-down menu in the lower righthand corner of the serial monitor.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215f9dd2e7\" name=\"6a2215f9dd2e7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>If statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Next up and very important: the command that will actually read the data from the serial line. You&#8217;ll be using an if statement to do this, and it will be inside\u00a0void loop ().<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">if (Serial.available() &gt; 0)<\/pre>\n<p>This statement will be true if the serial line detects any message with the same baud rate. You&#8217;ll be using your computer to send messages to your Smart Inventor Board, and those will be displayed on the serial monitor.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215f9dd340\" name=\"6a2215f9dd340\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Serial.print()<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The next line of code will have your serial monitor doing some printing! Don&#8217;t worry &#8212; you won&#8217;t need a printer with ink and paper for this. Type the line of code below within the if statement&#8217;s curly brackets:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">{\r\nSerial.println( (char) Serial.read() );\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>This prints, or displays, a new line with whatever characters (char for short) you typed in the serial monitor and clicked send with.<\/p>\n<p>One thing you can do with this is control the Smart Inventor Board with your computer acting as a controller. You could use the char read to activate a command, like driving a motor or turning on an LED.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215f9dd39a\" name=\"6a2215f9dd39a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The final code should look like this:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void setup(){\r\n\r\nSerial.begin(57600);\r\n\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop(){\r\n\r\n    if (Serial.available() &gt; 0)\r\n        {\r\n            Serial.println( (char) Serial.read() );\r\n        }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>Upload your code to your board, open up the serial monitor, and follow what the video does. The board should repeat whatever you type into the serial monitor![\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215f9dd3e0\" name=\"6a2215f9dd3e0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Want to see the lesson in action? Watch the video![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=a3R9kqgtZ-E&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 7 Setup [vc_column_text]For this lesson, you're going to be sending a message from your computer to your Smart Inventor Board. Because you'll be reading serial data, you will&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-serial-read\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1732,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1760,1777,1808,1793,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,171],"lesson-tag":[2163,2123,2182,2122,2171],"class_list":["post-1446","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-if-statements","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","module-programming","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1446","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1446\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1449,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1446\/revisions\/1449"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1732"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1446"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1446"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1446"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}